Subject: Remove lazy JSON.parse

What this does
  - removes the lazy JSON.parse of 0011 and its later extensions: the tape document class, the JS_TAG_LAZY_JSON marker, every marker test and materialisation on property, element and cache paths (interpreter, register VM, inline caches, AOT runtime helpers), the QJS_JSON_LAZY environment switch, the runtime's json_lazy_enabled and lazy_json_seen fields and their AOT layout entries (tag_lazy_json, off_rt_lazy_json)
  - JS_VALUE_HAS_REF_COUNT loses its marker exclusion (both encodings)
  - JS_SetJSONLazyEnabled stays as a documented no-op for API compatibility

Why we need it
  Owner decision (MSG 984). After 0581-0599 the eager parser is as fast as the lazy one's up-front pass and lazy was slower everywhere measured: parse only 0.97-1.04x eager, a few reads 1.05-1.06x, a full walk 1.93-2.17x (documents of 14 KB and 506 KB). The marker tests cost on every property and element read and every reference count test.
  A removal patch rather than an edit of 0011 in place: 24 later patches touch the lazy code, and editing 0011 would have to be carried through each of them.

Soundness
  Nothing creates a marker any more (the only producer, the tape parser, is gone), so every removed test was false, and every removed materialisation unreachable. The AOT generator stops emitting its marker tests and the lazy-document flag checks in the same change (tools/aot/qjsaot); a unit generated by an older generator does not compile against this layout (QJS_AOT_TAG_LAZY_JSON and QJS_AOT_OFF_RT_LAZY_JSON are no longer defined, and the layout hash changes). JSON differentials (14 suites) identical to the previous engine.

